<item>
            <title>[IGNITE-17003] SqlDataTypesCoverageTests.testDecimalDataType failes flaky</title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IGNITE-17003</link>
                <project id="12315922" key="IGNITE">Ignite</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;There is a problem with this critical test - when start full test class there is high posibuility to get error on first tests. By default first test is testDecimalDataType. Every time I get different errors - it makes a suggestion about side effect of started cluster. Test doesn&#8217;t fail starting separately. &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;Case of fail: &lt;span class=&quot;error&quot;&gt;&amp;#91;atomicityMode=ATOMIC, cacheMode=PARTITIONED, ttlFactory=null, backups=2, evictionFactory=null, onheapCacheEnabled=false, writeSyncMode=FULL_ASYNC, persistenceEnabled=false&amp;#93;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Root cause:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br/&gt;
The test is invalid for {{FULL_ASYNC }}mode. &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;The sequential execute&lt;br/&gt;
UPDATE &#8230;&lt;br/&gt;
SELECT &#8230;&lt;br/&gt;
cannot guarantee visibility UPDATE changes for the SELECT query when FULL_ASYNC mode is used.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;&lt;b&gt;Possible fixes:&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br/&gt;
There can be two ways:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;    don&#8217;t use FULL_ASYNC mode at the test. &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;    wait for UPDATE changes is applied.&lt;/p&gt;

</description>
